                <pb facs="0798" n="700" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg700"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.00 Revolutions/8: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Curtis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-02-25T10:00:00-04:40">February 25, 1930—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:50 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>15. The information contained in my 14, February 24, 11 p.m., although obtained
                    from the Government and acted upon by it, was <pb facs="0799" n="701"
                        xml:id="pg701"/> incorrect; the revolutionists have not advanced but are
                    awaiting result of Cabot’s negotiations in Santiago. I am hopeful but consider
                    the presence of a war vessel a desirable precaution.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Curtis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
